# Uniform-random path corpus for the published benchmark matrix.
#
# This is the w = 3 instance (the base cell's 1,000 routes) of a generated
# family: corpus::path_expr(PathCorpus::UniformRandom, routes) derives the
# regex for any other power-of-ten route count by substituting the digit
# count in the {3} group below. Paired with the Flat route shape
# (corpus::route_table): every expansion of this regex names exactly one
# route in that table.
#
# Any tool that expands this pattern with an unbounded repetition operator
# (this one has none) must pass --max-repeat 4, so a future edit that adds
# one is still bounded. See MAX_REGEX_REPEAT in crates/irontraffic-bench/src/corpus.rs.
/api/v1/r[0-9]{3}/[0-9a-f]{8}
